@prefix rdf:         <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh:          <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd:         <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema:      <http://schema.org/>.
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>.
@prefix cdifd: <https://cdif.org/validation/0.1/shacl#> .
@base <https://www.ogc.org/rules/template/> .

# xasOptional is the fully-optional XAS tier: it imposes no requirements, so
# there is deliberately no shape here.
#
# XasOptionalConformsToShape used to advise (sh:Warning) that a record using
# optional XAS fields should declare conformance to the optional tier. It was
# removed for two reasons. It had stopped working: its SPARQL target selected on
# schema:additionalType being the string literal "dcat:CatalogRecord", and records
# now carry {"@id": "dcat:CatalogRecord"}, which expands to an IRI -- so the target
# matched nothing and the advisory fired on no document at all. And the advice was
# not worth restoring: this module declares no `required`, so conformance to
# xasOptional/1.0 is satisfied vacuously by every document and detect_conformance
# has no rule that can check the claim.
#
# The JSON Schema twin of the same rule is gone from schema.yaml; see the note there.
